WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.954
CompTIA Network Plus, domain 3, Network operations, which is 19 percent of the exam.

00:00:07.954 --> 00:00:10.719
This lesson covers objective 3 point 3.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:13.200
Explain disaster-recovery concepts.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.020
Today: which recovery point objective needs synchronous replication?

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.900
R P O stands for recovery point objective.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.490
It is how much data you can afford to lose, measured back from the failure.

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.580
The gap between the last good copy and the failure is the data you lose.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:37.570
To make that gap zero, every write must reach the replica before it counts as done.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.989
That's synchronous replication.

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:43.560
A zero R P O accepts no data loss, so it requires it.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:46.689
Lock this in.

00:00:46.689 --> 00:00:49.298
R P O is how much data loss you can accept.

00:00:49.298 --> 00:00:54.637
Zero means none, and the only way to get zero is to replicate every write synchronously.

00:00:54.637 --> 00:00:56.760
That's objective three point three.
